  "id": "tactile-stimulation",
  "term": "tactile stimulation",
  "definition": "Tactile stimulation is sensory input produced by touch, including contact with different textures and levels of pressure on the skin. In psychology, it is described as a strong sensory experience that can shape emotional responses and well-being, with soft or smooth touch often linked to comfort, relaxation, and reduced stress.",
